  <h2>About procurement in Mpumalanga</h2>
  <p>
    Mpumalanga's procurement environment is shaped by the Highveld coal-power complex, the Lowveld tourism
    and agriculture sector, and three district municipalities covering everything from urban Emalahleni to
    the rural areas bordering eSwatini and Mozambique. The province runs procurement through departments
    coordinated by the Mpumalanga Provincial Treasury.
  </p>

  <h2>Key procuring entities</h2>

  <h3>Provincial departments</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mpumalanga Department of Public Works, Roads and Transport</strong> — provincial roads, buildings, scholar transport.</li>
    <li><strong>Mpumalanga Department of Health</strong> — Witbank, Rob Ferreira, and district hospitals.</li>
    <li><strong>Mpumalanga Department of Education</strong> — school infrastructure and stationery.</li>
    <li><strong>Mpumalanga Department of Agriculture, Rural Development, Land and Environmental Affairs</strong> — agri-infrastructure, fencing.</li>
    <li><strong>Mpumalanga Department of Human Settlements</strong> — housing developments.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Municipalities</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>District municipalities: <strong>Ehlanzeni, Gert Sibande, Nkangala</strong>.</li>
    <li>Constituent locals include <strong>Mbombela (Nelspruit), Emalahleni (Witbank), Govan Mbeki (Secunda), Steve Tshwete (Middelburg), Bushbuckridge</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where Mpumalanga tenders are advertised</h2>
  <p>
    All provincial and municipal tenders appear on the
    <a href="https://www.etenders.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eTenders Publication Portal</a>.
    The Mpumalanga Provincial Treasury publishes annual procurement plans.
  </p>

  <h2>What sets Mpumalanga apart</h2>
  <p>
    The province sits at the centre of South Africa's <strong>Just Energy Transition</strong> conversation.
    The phase-down of coal-fired power stations is generating tenders for repurposing, decommissioning,
    skills development, and renewable energy installations. The Lowveld's
    <strong>tourism, agriculture, and forestry economies</strong> drive a different stream of tenders
    around the Kruger National Park boundary and the Mbombela area.
  </p>

  <h2>Bidding strategy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>For energy-transition adjacent work, ensure your CSD profile includes renewable energy and decommissioning service codes.</li>
    <li>The mining and power-station industrial corridor offers significant subcontracting opportunities for SMMEs in services.</li>
    <li>Watch the Mbombela and Govan Mbeki municipal pipelines — they have the largest revenue bases in the province.</li>
  </ul>
</TenderHubLayout>
